look into the protection racket.  and try it with all characters. this
made the difference for me, since you learn to really get the most out
of your pet, completely empty stores, and hit -10 ac really quickly.
keeping your own level down and knowing how to survive with little HP/
PW also means monsters are less dangerous, and you learn to be
careful.

having a plan is a good idea.  are you going to hit the mines for the
tools/shops/temple first, oracle for some spoilers, sokoban for wands,
food, and fairly often a unihorn in addition to the end prize?

another thing that really helped was (in numpad movement) 5 +
direction when running.  this will run you until you hit something
interesting, and is a good way to move around without accidentally
hitting things you don't want to hit.

knowing how many traps are on certain levels can help you know how
often to search or watch where you pet moves and doesn't until you
find them all.


